load @term/seed/structure/set
  find set

# A process algebra: an algebra of concurrent processes, with operators for running in sequence, in parallel, and in
# choice, and an equational theory for when two processes behave the same (bisimulation). It is the algebraic face of
# concurrency, the counterpart of Petri nets and transition systems. The form carries the set of processes.
form process-algebra
  link processes, like set
